course: dictionary
lesson: 4485
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Hat is a good example. Most of the time it means the thing you wear on your head. «Hats off to» someone is a phrase, and together those words mean well done.
explain: Read the sentence around the word to find which meaning is used. In «spent every one of Ollie's coins on a hat shaped like a slice of toast», the hat is something you buy, because the sentence talks about coins. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Words in other languages have clues too. In French, «un chapeau» means a hat. The ending -eau is a clue: words ending in -eau are almost always masculine, so you say «un», not «une».
fact: A hat is something you wear on your head.
fact: Hats keep you warm in winter and keep the sun off you in summer.
fact: «Wear a different hat» means to have a different job or role.
fact: «Hats off to» someone means well done to them.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «no hat, no play» is a sun-safety rule at many schools.
exercise: Mia put on her warm hat before going out in the snow. Why did she wear it? | To hold her books | To pay for the bus | *To keep her head warm | To make her run faster
exercise: Jamal is a teacher on weekdays, but on Saturdays he wears a different hat: he coaches football. What does «wears a different hat» mean? | He is wearing a new hat | He wants a bigger hat | *He has a different job or role | He lost his hat at school
exercise: «Hats off to Sam for finishing the race!» What does this mean? | *Well done to Sam | Sam lost the race | Sam needs a new hat | Sam must take his hat off
test: «Un chapeau» is a hat. Which ending is a clue that a French word is masculine? | -s | -ing | -ette | *-eau
test: In the phrase «hats off to», what does hat mean? | It means a hat you take off to say hello | It means a party hat | It means a shop that sells hats | *The phrase means well done
exam: Which sentence uses hat to mean a job or role? | «Lily bought a sun hat for the beach.» | «Ben wore his hard hat on the building site.» | *«Ana wears many hats: she is a nurse, a mum and a runner.» | «The magician pulled a rabbit out of his hat.»
